<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25554" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăcīnĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακίνιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a promontory in Magna Græcia, near
				Crotona, with a temple to Juno</i>, now <i>Capo
				delle Colonne</i> or <i>Cape Nao</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27,
			25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">36, 42</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 10, 15, § 96</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăcīnĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Lacinium, Lacinian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Juno,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 24, 48</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 24, 3, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2,
				107, 111, § 240</span></i>; <i><span class="en">35, 9, 36, §
			64</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diva,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Juno</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 552</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					15, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 15, 701</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
